{"id":"8a92834baa408892323d4dc67c6c140c5fac6f03","axis":"silent","repo":"TryGhost/Ghost","sha":"8a92834baa408892323d4dc67c6c140c5fac6f03","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"ghost/core/boot.js","lines":["@@ -162,7 +162,7 @@ async function initCore({ ghostServer, config }) {","   debug('End: i18n');"," ","   // Reads admin_session_secret, so it follows settings. Under legacy nothing loads","-  // Better Auth or reads its tables.","+  // Better Auth itself.","   if (config.get('auth:engine') === 'better-auth') {","     debug('Begin: Better Auth');","     await require('./server/auth').betterAuth.init();"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/README.md","lines":["@@ -13,16 +13,17 @@ builds the instance after settings and refuses to start on SQLite or without"," `auth:betterAuthDev`."," "," `auth:betterAuthDev` (default `false`) decides whether Ghost keeps Better","-Auth's data, under either engine: boot seeds credential rows from","-`users.password`. It only applies where the in-development tables exist, and","-boot refuses it elsewhere. It's hidden from generated config docs, and it's an","-opt-in separate from `createInDevelopmentTables` because the published","-`config.development.json` turns that on, and an older Ghost-CLI local install","-runs as development; such an install gets the tables but no copies of its","-password hashes. The testing configs and the monorepo's","-`ghost/config.development.json` turn it on. Boot creates the tables before","-anything reads them, so these checks read config rather than the database; they","-and the flag go away when the tables get a migration.","+Auth's data, under either engine: boot seeds credential rows and the legacy","+engine stores passwords in them (see [Passwords](#passwords)). It only applies","+where the in-development tables exist, and boot refuses it elsewhere. It's","+hidden from generated config docs, and it's an opt-in separate from","+`createInDevelopmentTables` because the published `config.development.json`","+turns that on, and an older Ghost-CLI local install runs as development; such","+an install gets the tables but keeps its passwords in `users.password`. The","+testing configs and the monorepo's `ghost/config.development.json` turn it on.","+Boot creates the tables before anything reads them, so these checks read config","+rather than the database; they and the flag go away when the tables get a","+migration."," "," Under `better-auth` the Admin API serves the handler on `/auth/*`"," (`web/api/endpoints/admin/better-auth.ts`), after the private cache header and ahead of body parsing because","@@ -32,8 +33,7 @@ credential route counts against its compatibility route's limiters, sharing"," their counters, and a successful sign-in or password reset clears `userLogin`"," as the compatibility routes do. `/change-password` and `/verify-password`,"," which check the current password, count against `globalBlock` under their own","-paths. `/change-password` stays disabled until legacy sign-in reads","-`user_accounts` (plan Phase 2). Other paths are not limited. An after-hook strips","+paths. Other paths are not limited. An after-hook strips"," session tokens from native response bodies, by shape: a top-level `token`,"," `session.token`, and each list item's `token`. The token still travels in the"," `httpOnly` session cookie, and server-side `auth.api` calls keep it. Origin","@@ -86,6 +86,47 @@ IPv6 counts per /64, the block a single subscriber usually holds.","   it with `auth:betterAuthDev`; it skips users that already have one."," - `enabled.ts`: `usesBetterAuth()`, which throws where `auth:betterAuthDev`","   is on without the tables. Boot's seeder calls it, so that fails boot.","+- `credential-password.ts`: the legacy engine's password store. See","+  [Passwords](#passwords).","+","+## Passwords","+","+Both engines hash with bcrypt and read and write the same `credential` row in","+`user_accounts` with `auth:betterAuthDev` (plan §4.5), so a password changed","+through one engine works in the other. There is no dual write: `users.password`","+holds the `!` placeholder once the row has the hash, and only users the seeder","+copied still carry their old hash there, unread.","+","+- The `User` model hashes in `onSaving`, then `onSaved` writes the row with","+  the save's transaction, inserting it for a new user. `add`, `changePassword`","+  and `edit` with a password open a transaction when the caller has none.","+  Setup, invitations, imports, resets and `lock()` all save through the model.","+- Sign-in, `changePassword`'s current-password check and reset tokens","+  (`auth/passwordreset.ts`) read the hash from the row. A reset token is signed","+  with the hash, so a password change through either engine invalidates it.","+- A user without a credential row has no password.","+","+Without `auth:betterAuthDev` (the default, and always in production until the","+table graduates), all of this uses `users.password` as before.","+","+> [!WARNING]","+> With the flag on, the credential row is the only copy of a user's current","+> password. On a development database, anything that drops it or stops reading","+> it can lock users out or bring back an old password:","+>","+> - **Turning `auth:betterAuthDev` off** puts `users.password` back in use as","+>   it stands. A user whose password changed through legacy has the `!`","+>   placeholder there and can't sign in. A seeded user whose password changed","+>   only through Better Auth signs in with their old password.","+> - **Turning it back on** keeps any credential rows left from before, so a","+>   password changed while it was off is ignored for those users.","+> - **`pnpm gx db rebuild-development-tables`** drops `user_accounts`. The","+>   seeder then copies `users.password`, placeholders included, so anyone","+>   whose password changed is locked out.","+>","+> There's no migration path between these states. Reset the database instead","+> (`pnpm reset:db`, or `pnpm reset:data` for generated content), or reset the","+> affected users' passwords."," "," ## Tables"," "],"additions":53,"deletions":12,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/create-auth.ts","lines":["@@ -165,8 +165,6 @@ export function createAuth(deps: CreateAuthDeps) {","       '/change-email',","       '/delete-user',","       '/sign-in/social',","-      // Writes `user_accounts`, which legacy sign-in doesn't read until Phase 2","-      '/change-password',","     ],","     hooks: {","       after: createAuthMiddleware(async (ctx) => {"],"additions":0,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/credential-password.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@","+import type { Knex } from 'knex';","+import { usesBetterAuth } from './enabled';","+import { generateGhostId } from './ghost-models';","+","+// Legacy password store (plan §4.5): the `credential` row in `user_accounts`","+// with auth:betterAuthDev, otherwise `users.password`","+","+/** `users.password` once the credential row holds the hash; never a valid bcrypt hash */","+export const PASSWORD_PLACEHOLDER = '!';","+","+/**","+ * The user's password hash. A user without a credential row gets the","+ * placeholder, which no password matches.","+ */","+export async function readPasswordHash(","+  executor: Knex,","+  user: { id: string; password?: string | null },","+  { forUpdate = false }: { forUpdate?: boolean } = {},","+): Promise<string> {","+  if (!usesBetterAuth()) {","+    return user.password ?? PASSWORD_PLACEHOLDER;","+  }","+","+  const query = executor('user_accounts')","+    .where({ provider_id: 'credential', account_id: user.id })","+    .first('password');","+  const account = await (forUpdate ? query.forUpdate() : query);","+  return account?.password ?? PASSWORD_PLACEHOLDER;","+}","+","+/**","+ * Stores a user's new hash in their credential row, creating it if missing.","+ * Pass the user write's transaction so both commit together.","+ *","+ * Not an upsert: `ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE` takes next-key locks that deadlock","+ * concurrent user inserts in MySQL. `isNew` skips straight to the insert.","+ */","+export async function writePasswordHash(","+  executor: Knex,","+  userId: string,","+  hash: string,","+  { isNew = false }: { isNew?: boolean } = {},","+): Promise<void> {","+  const now = new Date();","+  if (!isNew) {","+    const updated = await executor('user_accounts')","+      .where({ provider_id: 'credential', account_id: userId })","+      .update({ password: hash, updated_at: now });","+    if (updated) {","+      return;","+    }","+  }","+","+  await executor('user_accounts').insert({","+    id: generateGhostId(),","+    user_id: userId,","+    account_id: userId,","+    provider_id: 'credential',","+    password: hash,","+    created_at: now,","+    updated_at: now,","+  });","+}"],"additions":63,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/enabled.ts","lines":["@@ -4,9 +4,9 @@ import { shouldCreateInDevelopmentTables } from '../../data/schema/in-developmen"," "," /**","  * Whether Ghost keeps Better Auth's data under either engine (auth:betterAuthDev):","- * boot seeds credential rows from `users.password`. Opt-in, so an install","- * that only has the in-development tables (an old Ghost-CLI local install runs","- * as development) doesn't copy its password hashes into them.","+ * boot seeds credential rows and the legacy engine stores passwords in them.","+ * Opt-in, so an install that only has the in-development tables (an old","+ * Ghost-CLI local install runs as development) leaves its passwords alone.","  * Boot's seeder calls this, so a misconfiguration fails boot.","  */"," export function usesBetterAuth(): boolean {"],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/knex-adapter.ts","lines":["@@ -32,7 +32,6 @@ export type KnexAdapterOptions = {"," };"," "," type Row = Record<string, 